Q: How to add a button to the Azure AD B2C custom policy and check the flow A: <p>Your <code>phoneSignUp_v1</code> content definition loads <code>selfAsserted.cshtml</code>, so swap it for your own HTML on blob storage and add a link that restarts the journey with a different domain hint:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;a href=&quot;https://yourtenant.b2clogin.com/yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com/B2C_1A_YourPolicy/oauth2/v2.0/authorize?...&amp;domain_hint=passkey&quot;&gt;
  Login with biometric
&lt;/a&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Then branch on <code>domain_hint</code> with a precondition, the way your <code>SocialLogin</code> subjourney already does with <code>isDomainHint</code>. There's also a bug worth fixing in <code>PassKeyFederation</code>. Your exchange IDs are crossed:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ClaimsExchange Id=&quot;PassKeyExchange_login&quot; TechnicalProfileReferenceId=&quot;PassKey-FIOD2-Registration&quot; /&gt;
&lt;ClaimsExchange Id=&quot;PassKeyExchange_Registration&quot; TechnicalProfileReferenceId=&quot;PassKey-FIOD2-Login&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Login points at Registration and vice versa.</p>

Q: AngularJS ng-click fires twice A: <p>Elements wrapped one another, and this can cause trigger event twice or more.</p>
<p>So i used a simple CSS trick for this solution :</p>
<pre><code>.off{
   pointer-events:none;
}
</code></pre>
<p>I applied class <code>off</code> to an element correspond to click event.</p>
<p>Of course it's better that elements doesn't wrapp one another in web design.</p>
